---
layout: base.njk
title: Documents & Forms – The Wheatlands HOA
description: Wheatlands HOA governing documents, architectural change forms, fence requirements and resolutions.
permalink: /documents.html
---
{%- from "macros.njk" import pageHead, docList, docItem -%}
{{ pageHead("Documents & Forms", "Governing documents, request forms and Board resolutions for the Wheatlands HOA.") }}
<section class="section anchor" id="forms">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-head"><h2>Forms</h2><p>Please submit forms <b>before</b> starting any work. Questions? Contact the <a href="/contacts.html">property manager or a Board member</a>.</p></div>
    <div class="grid cols-2" style="gap:24px;align-items:start">
      {%- for f in documents.forms %}
      <div class="card">
        <h3>{{ f.title }}</h3>
        <div class="prose-inline" style="margin-bottom:1em">{{ f.description | md | safe }}</div>
        {% if f.file %}<ul class="doc-list">{{ docItem(f.file, f.file_label or f.title, f.file_note) }}</ul>{% endif %}
      </div>
      {%- endfor %}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
<section class="section alt anchor" id="governing">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="grid cols-2" style="gap:40px;align-items:start">
      <div>
        <h2>Governing documents</h2>
        {{ docList(documents.governing) }}
      </div>
      <div id="resolutions" class="anchor">
        <h2>Resolutions</h2>
        {{ docList(documents.resolutions) }}
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
<section class="section">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-head"><h2>Key rules</h2><p>Plain-language summaries. The full text from the Declaration is included below each one.</p></div>
    <div class="grid cols-2" style="gap:24px;align-items:start">
      <div class="card anchor" id="sec-808">
        <h3>Fences: Section 8.08(c)</h3>
        <p>On lots designated “Fence Restricted Lots,” a fence may be built only between the rear lot line and the back of the home, and must meet these specifications:</p>
        <ul class="spec">
          <li><b>Material</b><span>Western Red Cedar, board-on-board (shadow box)</span></li>
          <li><b>Height</b><span>4, 5 or 6 feet (per Board rules) and compliant with municipal code</span></li>
          <li><b>Boards</b><span>1×6, spaced edge-to-edge and back-to-back to meet the city’s percent-open requirement</span></li>
          <li><b>Posts</b><span>4×4 with cedar cap, set 42″ deep about 8 ft on center, concrete footings</span></li>
          <li><b>Rails</b><span>Two 2×4 back rails: one at the top of the boards, one 12″ up from the bottom</span></li>
          <li><b>Top cap</b><span>1×4, centered on the boards</span></li>
        </ul>
        <p class="small muted mb-0">Effective January 1, 2026, damaged fencing must be repaired promptly; unrepaired damage may be fined.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
